   "narrative": "In the west the merchants of Cologne already held privileges in England. In 1266 King Henry III granted the Hansa of Lübeck and Hamburg a charter of their own, and in 1282 the Cologne and Baltic groups joined to form a single Hanseatic colony in London, later known as the Steelyard, beside London Bridge. Bruges in Flanders became the other western pole of the trade. In the east the merchants twice blockaded Novgorod, in 1268 and 1277–1278, to defend their privileges there.",
