   "title": "Valdemar IV takes Gotland",
   "time": "1361–1362",
   "narrative": "In July 1361 King Valdemar IV of Denmark landed on Gotland and took Visby, opening a war with the Hanseatic towns over Gotland, Scania and the Sound. The Baltic towns struck back, but on 8 July 1362 the Danish fleet beat theirs off Helsingborg, and the Lübeck mayor Johann Wittenborg who had led it was later tried and executed at home. With the Sound contested, the herring fair in Scania and the voyages to Bergen were disrupted, and a truce in 1365 favoured Denmark.",
