   "time": "1391–1398",
   "narrative": "Between 1391 and 1398 Lübeck dug the Stecknitz Canal toward Lauenburg on the Elbe, giving Lüneburg salt a water route to its harbour. The Baltic had become unsafe: the Victual Brothers, privateers first hired in a war over the Swedish crown, seized Visby and preyed on shipping. In 1398 the Teutonic Order, backed by the Prussian towns, drove them out of Gotland, and that year a consortium of Hanseatic towns handed back Stockholm, which it had governed since 1395.",
